From fbcdb33a192d4b09273b8e9c0b1aa0191926259c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] refactor: validate state declarations from BaseStateMeta
 without module globals

The reserved-state-name check moves from reflex.istate.validation into
reflex_base.vars.base, next to the metaclass that runs it. BaseState declares
itself the root of its hierarchy with `state_root=True`; BaseStateMeta.__new__
stores the root on that class, finds it again on the bases of every class
created later and validates against the root's namespace. Nothing has to be
installed after the class body, and nothing is shared between roots: a second
root in the same process reserves only its own members. Classes with no root
among their bases (the root itself, EvenMoreBasicBaseState, plain models) are
left alone, as before.

Refs #7211

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
